        <mxCell id="llama_3_multi_modal-117" value="&lt;b&gt;Illustration of the compositional approach to adding multimodal capabilities to Llama 3 that we study in this paper.&lt;/b&gt; This approach leads to a multimodal model that is trained in five stages: &lt;b&gt;(1)&lt;/b&gt; language model pre-training, &lt;b&gt;(2)&lt;/b&gt; multi-modal encoder pre-training, &lt;b&gt;(3)&lt;/b&gt; vision adapter training, &lt;b&gt;(4)&lt;/b&gt; model finetuning, and &lt;b&gt;(5)&lt;/b&gt; speech adapter training." style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=20.2;fontColor=#000000;" vertex="1" parent="llama_3_multi_modal-figure">
