        <mxCell id="simplifying_transformer_blocks-94" value="Comparison between different Transformer blocks. (Left) The standard Pre-LN block. (Top Right) Our most simplified block. (Bottom Right) The parallel block (Zhao et al., 2019; Wang &amp;amp; Komatsuzaki, 2021). Like the parallel block, our block eschews the need for sequential sub-blocks, but we additionally remove all skip connections and normalisation layers, as well as value and projection parameters. Here, &lt;span style=&quot;font-family:DejaVu Sans,Segoe UI Symbol,Cambria Math,STIX Two Math,sans-serif;&quot;&gt;⊗&lt;/span&gt; denotes a matrix multiplication, and &lt;span style=&quot;font-family:DejaVu Sans,Segoe UI Symbol,Cambria Math,STIX Two Math,sans-serif;&quot;&gt;⊕&lt;/span&gt; denotes a (potentially weighted) sum." style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=20.1;fontColor=#000000;" vertex="1" parent="simplifying_transformer_blocks-figure">
          <mxGeometry x="0" y="433.3" width="948.75" height="128.6" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
