        <mxCell id="coconet-71" value="&lt;b&gt;Overview of &lt;span style=&quot;font-variant:small-caps;&quot;&gt;CoCoNet&lt;/span&gt;’s workflow. First, a user expresses a machine learning algorithm in the DSL that contains both computation (MatMul) and communication (AllReduce). Then, the autotuner applies transformations to optimize the program while keeping the algorithm unchanged, such as fusing AllReduce and Dropout into FusedAllReduce and overlapping this with MatMul. Finally, &lt;span style=&quot;font-variant:small-caps;&quot;&gt;CoCoNet&lt;/span&gt; generates custom communication and computation code, which is available through PyTorch.&lt;/b&gt;" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=21.9;fontColor=#000000;" vertex="1" parent="coconet-figure">
          <mxGeometry x="0" y="276.5" width="1475" height="113.1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
