        <mxCell id="gpt3_fig21-109" value="&lt;b&gt;Zero-shot, one-shot and few-shot, contrasted with traditional fine-tuning&lt;/b&gt;. The panels above show four methods for performing a task with a language model – fine-tuning is the traditional method, whereas zero-, one-, and few-shot, which we study in this work, require the model to perform the task with only forward passes at test time. We typically present the model with a few dozen examples in the few shot setting. Exact phrasings for all task descriptions, examples and prompts can be found in Appendix G." style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=16.9;fontColor=#000000;" vertex="1" parent="gpt3_fig21-figure">
