        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="graph_transformer_networks-378" value="Graph Transformer Networks (GTNs) learn to generate a set of new meta-path adjacency matrices 𝔸&lt;sup style=&quot;line-height:0;&quot;&gt;(&lt;i&gt;l&lt;/i&gt;)&lt;/sup&gt; using GT layers and perform graph convolution as in GCNs on the new graph structures. Multiple node representations from the same GCNs on multiple meta-path graphs are integrated by concatenation and improve the performance of node classification. ℚ&lt;sub style=&quot;vertical-align:-0.3em;line-height:0;&quot;&gt;1&lt;/sub&gt;&lt;sup style=&quot;margin-left:-0.56em;vertical-align:0.55em;line-height:0;&quot;&gt;(&lt;i&gt;l&lt;/i&gt;)&lt;/sup&gt; and ℚ&lt;sub style=&quot;vertical-align:-0.3em;line-height:0;&quot;&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;&lt;sup style=&quot;margin-left:-0.56em;vertical-align:0.55em;line-height:0;&quot;&gt;(&lt;i&gt;l&lt;/i&gt;)&lt;/sup&gt; ∈ &lt;b&gt;R&lt;/b&gt;&lt;sup style=&quot;line-height:0;&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;N&lt;/i&gt;×&lt;i&gt;N&lt;/i&gt;×&lt;i&gt;C&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/sup&gt; are intermediate adjacency tensors to compute meta-paths at the &lt;i&gt;l&lt;/i&gt;th layer." style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=18.3;fontColor=#000000;" vertex="1" parent="graph_transformer_networks-figure">
          <mxGeometry x="0" y="499.72" width="925.05" height="117.8" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
