        <mxCell id="group_normalization-181" value="&lt;b&gt;Normalization methods&lt;/b&gt;. Each subplot shows a feature map tensor, with &lt;i&gt;N&lt;/i&gt; as the batch axis, &lt;i&gt;C&lt;/i&gt; as the channel axis, and (&lt;i&gt;H&lt;/i&gt;,&amp;nbsp;&lt;i&gt;W&lt;/i&gt;) as the spatial axes. The pixels in blue are normalized by the same mean and variance, computed by aggregating the values of these pixels." style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=13.1;fontColor=#000000;" vertex="1" parent="group_normalization-figure">
          <mxGeometry x="0" y="248.1" width="883.85" height="39.4" as="geometry" />
