        <mxCell id="clip-107" value="Summary of our approach. While standard image models jointly train an image feature extractor and a linear classifier to predict some label, CLIP jointly trains an image encoder and a text encoder to predict the correct pairings of a batch of (image, text) training examples. At test time the learned text encoder synthesizes a zero-shot linear classifier by embedding the names or descriptions of the target dataset’s classes." style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=16.8;fontColor=#000000;" vertex="1" parent="clip-figure">
